{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":502327,"name":"Capital EyeMotors","username":"Capital_EyeMotors","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/c/db5fbb/{size}.png","created_at":"2026-09-28T02:17:49.269Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHi all. I run several Grok Bot assistants that share one Computer, and I update it manually from the Mac app (Settings \u0026gt; Updates \u0026gt; Update Grok Bot’s Computer). Two questions:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eThe help page (\u003ca href=\"http://cursor.com/help/grok-bot/computer-recovery\" class=\"inline-onebox\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003eGrok Bot computer | Cursor Docs\u003c/a\u003e) says an update can be run now “or scheduled for later.” Where is the scheduling option, and how does it work? I only see the Update button.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eThe “Automatic Updates” toggle in Settings says it updates the client. Is there a separate option that updates the Computer automatically when it’s idle? (I noticed an autoUpdateWhenIdleOptIn value set to false in the Computer’s settings, but couldn’t find a matching toggle in the app.)\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI’d like the Computer to update at a quiet time, like overnight or weekends, without needing someone to press the button. Thanks!\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":2,"updated_at":"2026-09-28T02:17:55.121Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":11,"reads":2,"readers_count":1,"score":55.4,"yours":false,"topic_id":173167,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-computer-updates-is-there-an-automatic-or-scheduled-option","display_username":"Capital EyeMotors","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":2,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"http://cursor.com/help/grok-bot/computer-recovery","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"Grok Bot computer | Cursor Docs","clicks":0}],"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":139960,"hidden":false,"trust_level":0,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grok-bot-computer-updates-is-there-an-automatic-or-scheduled-option/173167/1","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null,"can_vote":false},{"id":502479,"name":"Mohit","username":"mohitjain","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/mohitjain/{size}/100229_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-28T08:37:08.121Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHey \u003ca class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/capital_eyemotors\"\u003e@Capital_EyeMotors\u003c/a\u003e!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e1. Scheduling. That option isn’t on your account yet, so the Update button is all you’ll see for now. The help page is a bit ahead of itself there, sorry for the confusion. When it does arrive it lets you set a daily time (not specific days, so no weekends-only), with an option to auto-apply future updates too.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e2. Automatic Updates toggle. That one, and the \u003ccode\u003eautoUpdateWhenIdleOptIn\u003c/code\u003e value you found, only updates the Grok Bot app, not the Computer. There’s no “update the Computer when idle” switch today. It can self-update once it’s sat idle long enough to sleep, but you can’t time it, and with several assistants sharing one Computer it rarely gets that gap.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSo the reliable path is still pressing Update at a quiet time. You can do that from the iPhone app too, so no one has to be at the Mac. I’ve passed along the ask for scheduled/overnight updates.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":6,"pos